# Firebase config for KY — Phase 3 (accounts + analytics).
#
# 1. Create a project at https://console.firebase.google.com
# 2. Add a Web App to it, copy the config values below.
# 3. Authentication -> Sign-in method -> enable Google, and enable GitHub
#    (GitHub needs an OAuth App at https://github.com/settings/developers;
#    set its callback URL to the one Firebase shows on the GitHub provider screen).
# 4. Firestore Database -> create database, then deploy firestore.rules from this repo.
# 5. Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values below. Vite only exposes
#    vars prefixed VITE_ to the client, and .env.local is git-ignored.
#
# None of these values are secret — they identify the Firebase project, they do
# not authorize access on their own — but keep them out of the committed history
# anyway so the project id isn't hard-coded into the OSS repo.
# Leaving this file (or .env.local) unset is fine: the app runs local-only, exactly
# as it did before Phase 3 — no sign-in, no cloud sync, no analytics.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
